course: dictionary
lesson: 15575
title: Swaggering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Swaggering is an adjective, a describing word. It comes from the verb swagger, which has forms swagger, swaggers, swaggered and swaggering. When you see swaggering, the words around it often show you what it means. «The swaggering pirate waved his sword and laughed loudly.» A pirate who waves his sword and laughs loudly wants everyone to notice him, so swaggering means proud and showing off.
explain: Look for the clues. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is the classic swaggering character, strutting about in his motor-car goggles and boasting in his songs. He is not just walking. He is showing off, and the author uses swaggering to tell you that.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The proud and showing-off pirate waved his sword», and if it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Swaggering can also mean too confident and boastful, so it often tells the reader that a character thinks too highly of himself.
fact: Swaggering means walking or behaving in a proud, show-off way, as if you are very important.
fact: Swaggering can also mean too confident and boastful.
fact: Swaggering is the adjective form of the verb swagger, which has the forms swagger, swaggers, swaggered and swaggering.
fact: «Swaggering» is often used for pirates, bullies and show-offs in stories.
fact: Toad in The Wind in the Willows is a classic swaggering character, boasting in his motor-car goggles.
exercise: «The swaggering pirate waved his sword and laughed loudly.» What does swaggering show about the pirate? | Sleepy and slow | Lost and scared | *Proud and showing off | Shy and quiet
exercise: Swaggering comes from which verb? | *swagger | swallow | swim | sway
exercise: «Tom swaggered up to the class, sure he had won, though he had not even tried.» What does swaggered suggest? | Hungry and cold | *Too confident and boastful | Lost in the crowd | Nervous and tired
test: «Toad swaggered around in his motor-car goggles, boasting to everyone.» Why is Toad described as swaggering? | Because he was lost | Because he was asleep | Because he was ill | *Because he acted proud and showed off
test: Which word means nearly the same as swaggering? | *Boastful | Shy | Hidden | Gentle
exam: «The swaggering bully strutted past the younger children, daring anyone to speak.» What is the best meaning of swaggering here? | Walking very slowly | Scared of everyone | *Proud and showing off, as if he is important | Happy to help others
